#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157189 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157369 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "697e5bea-20b4-5de0-9992-7a67ee932809" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Two-Branch PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "0a870e80-5a73-59d2-997f-bec2d9a947e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-7988" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac {10}{3},$ compute $\\textrm{Var}[X].$\n![](images/50/50e7428db936f89942d4c775d2dfe7691b853a9ca729e30c1958cb25b6c1e8d2.svg)" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E [X^2] - \\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\textrm E[X^2],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot (8-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(8{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2})|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{67}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{67}{6}-{(\\frac{10}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157190 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157370 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c834972a-1ed0-585c-803c-906fcea8cea8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Three-Branch PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "77bbf810-ec26-5224-9d3e-62de3e0529fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-7990" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function given below. Given that $\\textrm E[X]\\approx 1.791\\,67,$ compute $\\textrm{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n![](images/f6/f63c459b8c212033b5dbe5f0c3a4176b7f921788bed579e8615d1a3a3d9b3f17.svg)" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E [X^2] - \\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\textrm E[X^2]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{12}|}_{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4})|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & ≈4.041\\,67\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & ≈4.041\\,67-(1.791\\,67)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.83\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157369 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "697e5bea-20b4-5de0-9992-7a67ee932809" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Two-Branch PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31e8a360-bbb6-5ff2-b1db-6f35ee0fb9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430369} {:answer/id #uuid "497c8e24-3ed3-5e00-ac42-19805589f75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430372} {:answer/id #uuid "5f1cc211-5e0d-51fa-be2e-fd25ee32fb31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430375} {:answer/id #uuid "715e9c36-f6d8-592b-8bb2-6d5a3d196969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430378} {:answer/id #uuid "76363301-ac77-5722-bc0a-5eb853e83c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31e8a360-bbb6-5ff2-b1db-6f35ee0fb9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430369} :answer-field/id #uuid "83b0e856-ac3a-5380-970b-faca3f779b77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30cb3fc9-0bbc-51d2-bbe4-e74999cc9efd" :question/math-academy-id "q-90562" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{45})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{30})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}-{(\\frac{11}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{50} \\\\  & =0.66.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
